---
// origin: human. Written by Ken, not the pipeline. Static page by design (see /writing/).
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { essayBySlug, authorshipOf } from '../../../data/writing';
import { personKenAshe, websiteKenAshe } from '../../../data/schema';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../../consts';
import EssayFigure from '../../../components/EssayFigure.astro';
import { ogImageOf } from '../../../data/writing-images';

const essay = essayBySlug('you-can-use-ai-to-learn-almost-anything-even-ai');
const authorship = authorshipOf(essay);

const title = 'You Can Use AI to Learn Almost Anything. Even AI.';
const description =
  'I asked ChatGPT to build me a 30-day course with exercises, quizzes, and feedback instead of just answering questions. Here is how to turn it into a tutor for almost anything, and a starting prompt.';
// Social/schema image: a 1200px derivative of the essay's declared image (writing.ts).
const og = await ogImageOf(essay);

// Article node for this essay. Author and publisher are the canonical Person (imported, not
// forked: DECISIONS.md D9); the essay is human-directed, so unlike Digest posts the author
// is Ken Ashe himself. Same self-contained @graph pattern as every other content page.
// Maintained by hand, like ABOUT_DATE_MODIFIED: bump in the same commit as any material edit
// to the essay body. 2026-09-25: added the short video and its lead-in paragraph.
const ESSAY_DATE_MODIFIED = '2026-09-25';
const pageUrl = new URL(`/writing/you-can-use-ai-to-learn-almost-anything-even-ai/`, SITE_URL).toString();
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Article',
      '@id': `${pageUrl}#article`,
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      url: pageUrl,
      mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
      ...(og ? { image: new URL(og.src, SITE_URL).toString() } : {}),
      datePublished: essay.published,
      dateModified: ESSAY_DATE_MODIFIED,
      author: { '@id': 'https://kenashe.ai/#ken-ashe' },
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://kenashe.ai/#ken-ashe' },
      isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://kenashe.ai/#website' },
      inLanguage: 'en-US',
    },
    websiteKenAshe,
    personKenAshe,
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  image={og?.src}
  ogImageWidth={og?.width}
  ogImageHeight={og?.height}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Writing', path: '/writing/' },
    { name: title, path: '/writing/you-can-use-ai-to-learn-almost-anything-even-ai/' },
  ]}
>
  <JsonLd slot="jsonld" data={articleSchema} />
  <article class="essay">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/writing/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Writing</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="essay-header">
      <p class="page-mark" aria-hidden="true">// writing</p>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="meta">
        <span class="meta-key">By</span> Ken Ashe
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> September 14, 2026
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {authorship}
      </p>
    </header>

    <EssayFigure essay={essay} priority />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>I wanted to get better at using AI, so I asked ChatGPT to teach me.</p>
      <p>I did not just ask it questions. I asked it to build a 30-day course with practical exercises, quizzes, and feedback. About 30 minutes a day, focused on what I wanted to become able to do.</p>
      <p>The important instruction was simple: <strong>do not just explain the topic. Make me practice it.</strong></p>
      <p><strong>Prefer video?</strong> I recently made a short version of this idea: how I recommend getting started with AI without trying to learn everything at once.</p>
      <figure class="video">
        <div class="video-frame">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/iEjd1OvHLS0?playsinline=1"
            title="Ken Ashe: Getting started with AI"
            width="360"
            height="640"
            loading="lazy"
            allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            allowfullscreen
            referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <a href="https://youtube.com/shorts/iEjd1OvHLS0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube</a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>Turn it into a tutor</h2>
      <p>My course covered prompting, checking AI-generated answers, and the difference between workflows and agents.</p>
      <p>I asked ChatGPT to give me questions, wait for my answers, and explain what I got right or wrong. When I struggled with something, I wanted to revisit it rather than move on just to finish the schedule.</p>
      <p>Mastery, not pace.</p>
      <p>That was more useful to me than simply asking for explanations. I had to attempt something, examine the feedback, and ask follow-up questions when I did not understand.</p>
      <p>The model’s feedback still needed checking. A confident explanation or a passing score was not proof that either of us was right.</p>
      <h2>Try it with something you want to learn</h2>
      <p>You could use this approach to practice a language, understand a software tool, or explore a subject you have been putting off.</p>
      <p>Here is a starting prompt:</p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>Act as my tutor for [subject]. My goal is to [what I want to be able to do].</p>
        <p>Start by asking questions to assess what I already know. Then build a learning plan for about 30 minutes a day.</p>
        <p>Teach one concept at a time. Give me an exercise, wait for my answer, and explain what I got right or wrong. Revisit the parts I struggle with. Include practical tasks and sources I can check.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>Your answers give you something to work with. Ask for another example, challenge the feedback, or try a harder exercise.</p>
      <h2>Change the lessons when your goals change</h2>
      <p>I eventually stopped following my original curriculum because I wanted to focus on agents that use tools and complete tasks. I changed the training to match.</p>
      <p>The earlier program was still useful. I did not need to finish it just because it was the original plan.</p>
      <p><strong>You do not have to use AI only to do things for you. You can use it to help you learn how to do them yourself.</strong></p>
      <p>I started with AI. The subject you choose is up to you.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .essay {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .crumbs {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .crumbs a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 150ms ease;
  }
  .crumbs a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .page-mark {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .essay-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .meta-key {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .meta span[aria-hidden] {
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .prose {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .prose li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .prose blockquote p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose blockquote p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  /* Portrait video (YouTube Short): a 9:16 box reserves the space before the lazy iframe
     loads, capped at 360px and centered; the frame is never cropped or letterboxed. */
  .prose .video {
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 360px;
  }
  .prose .video-frame {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--border);
  }
  .prose .video-frame iframe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }
  .prose .video figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
